I always took it as not mi'a but mi - which in Lojban has a referent that
is the speaker, but if you're speaking on behalf of a group means that
group (but not also others), just as a group can be do if that's who you're
addressing. Now, it's unclear how big a group you're speaking for in that
prayer (I interpret it as roda), but those "we"s and "us"es never contrast
with a smaller "me."

